cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Deepfake Generalization: shortcut-controlled multimodal deepfake detection"
abstract: >-
  A research platform testing whether cue-specific fusion of visual artifacts,
  audio spoofing and mouth-audio alignment generalizes better than a strong
  visual baseline, under source-disjoint and shortcut-controlled evaluation.
  The contribution is the validity protocol rather than the accuracy: the
  measured answer on this data is negative and is reported with its intervals.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
license-url: "https://github.com/vaibhavshiroorkar/deepfake-generalization/blob/main/LICENSE.md"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vaibhavshiroorkar/deepfake-generalization"
keywords:
  - deepfake detection
  - multimodal fusion
  - generalization
  - shortcut learning
  - model calibration

